.TH ADD\-APT\-REPOSITORY 1 "October 2026" "menta-sources" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
add\-apt\-repository, apt\-add\-repository \- add or remove an APT repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B add\-apt\-repository
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I REPOSITORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B add\-apt\-repository
adds a repository to
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/additional\-repositories.list ,
or removes an existing one from any source file.
It must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes to all queries.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remove
Remove the repository instead of adding it.
.SH REPOSITORY STRING
.I REPOSITORY
is either a line in the
.BR sources.list (5)
one\-line format, for instance
.PP
.RS
deb [signed\-by=/usr/share/keyrings/example.gpg] https://example.com/debian trixie main
.RE
.PP
or a short form made of a URL followed by components, which is expanded
with the codename of the running Debian release:
.PP
.RS
add\-apt\-repository "https://example.com/debian main contrib"
.RE
.PP
PPAs are built for Ubuntu and are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR menta\-sources (1)
